   "widgets_values": [
    "subject_definitions:\n<Video 1> is the exact continuous BG_01 telecine motion control for global frames 300 through 542 (243 frames). It is the sole authority in every output frame for timing, frame order, camera state, architecture, every visible figure's silhouette, hat and torso angle, arms, legs, scale, screen position, depth order, reveal, overlap and occlusion.\n<Picture 1>, <Picture 2> and <Picture 3> are exact-pose synthetic appearance guides for global frames 340, 400 and 500, which are frames 41, 101 and 201 of this 243-frame video. All three are inside this video window. They share one photographic look.\n\nsummary:\n[video editing + reference generation] Reconstruct all 243 frames through one raw video-to-video diffusion trajectory. Follow <Video 1> for every frame-specific camera movement and geometric relationship. Use the pictures as appearance evidence at their exact instants and carry their single shared photographic look uniformly through every frame.\n\nretention_analysis:\nPreserve all 243 source frames in order and exact motion phase from BG_01. Do not hold, average, anticipate, delay, repeat, delete, retime, interpolate, stabilize, reframe, crop or redesign movement. Prefer Video 1 geometry over any still whenever they disagree.\n\ndetailed_description:\nPreserve the complete rounded film aperture shown in the pictures, with black outside it, and the rustic plaster-and-timber architecture supplied by the motion source. Preserve every visible person exactly as posed in the motion source. Render every frame with the pictures' look: correctly exposed black-and-white 16mm film with rich natural blacks, light grey textured plaster instead of blown-out white, highlights that roll off without clipping, and the same restrained fine grain and focus across people, walls, timber and ground. The washed-out, overexposed tonality of Video 1 is a transfer defect: do not reproduce it. Do not add scratches, dust, flicker or damage. Do not invent faces, props, people, text, color shifts or camera movement beyond what the source provides.\n",
    768,
    432,
    243,
    "match"
   ],
   "size": [
    400,
    502
   ],
   "title": "Reference to video: the prompt is the whole instruction"
  },
