   "title": "Reconstruction: El Tinterillo, stairs, window w3b (frames 300\u2013542)",
   "properties": {},
   "widgets_values": [
    "## What this graph does\n\nThe shot survives only as a damaged 16mm print and a soft telecine. The **hybrid** window (`tools/make_hybrid.py`: the median-cleaned 16mm frame with the registered telecine inside it) is the **motion control**: it decides timing, camera, every silhouette and the architecture. Three **reference stills** made from the hybrid (an image generator, prompt in `reference/reference_prompt.txt`) are the **appearance** at frames the three window frames named in the prompt. **MiniMax H3** reconstructs the window through them.\n\n**Output.** `stairs_w3b_*.mp4` at 768 \u00d7 432, 24 fps. Four such windows overlap and are joined by `tools/seam_blend.py` at cuts 200, 340 and 400."
   ],
   "color": "#3b3b2e",
   "bgcolor": "#5a5a3a"
  },
  {
   "id": 21,
   "type": "MarkdownNote",
   "pos": [
    0,
    318
   ],
   "size": [
    560,
    278
   ],
   "flags": {},
   "order": 20,
   "mode": 0,
   "inputs": [],
   "outputs": [],
   "title": "What should and should not happen",
   "properties": {},
   "widgets_values": [
    "**Should.** All frames of the window in order and in the hybrid's exact motion phase; the rounded film aperture; correctly exposed black-and-white with blacks that are black and plaster that is grey, not blown out; one look for the whole reel.\n\n**Should not.** Holding, averaging, retiming or stabilising the movement; invented faces, props, people or text; scratches, dust or flicker reproduced from the print; the washed-out tonality of the telecine reproduced as if it were the film. Small faces and lip movement are the known limit at this resolution.\n\n**What it is.** A reconstruction, with detail the film no longer holds, and labelled as one. The original scan and every raw window are kept."
   ],
   "color": "#3b3b2e",
   "bgcolor": "#5a5a3a"
  },
  {
